From ef0b8fe68c05d59c2df93a5801716318af506eac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:00:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vendorapk): add the vendor's apk-based distributions

Adds two OS families backed by the vendor's OSV advisory feed and keyed on
the os-release ID: the Linux distribution and its hardened container images
(for BellSoft: alpaquita and bellsoft-hardened-containers).

Both are apk-based and identify themselves through /etc/os-release, so the
generic os-release analyzer recognises them. Releases are the rolling
"stream" plus the numbered LTS branches 23 and 25; VERSION_ID is used
verbatim as the advisory release key. "stream" never reaches end of life;
the LTS branches are checked against their end of commercial support.

Advisories are stored as vulnerable version ranges and evaluated as
constraints with apk version semantics; an advisory that records when a
vulnerability was introduced but never fixed applies to every version from
that point on.

Advisories are keyed on the source package name, usually the apk origin.
Packages published under another name (the vendor's JDK: origin
"liberica21-lite", feed "openjdk21-lite", provides
"openjdk21-lite-jdk-no-deps") are resolved through the provided names with
the subpackage suffix stripped, from the package metadata alone.
